code:native-item:prt_1b037f0b5001cDDpsbnPr8Q4Ol", "threadId": "thread:project:7b60eb1e-933f-470d-b2e1-b9eeadaf3a8f:d3c439b9-0267-4e99-8dc3-36f6f0f4d997", "runId": "run:thread:thread%3Aproject%3A7b60eb1e-933f-470d-b2e1-b9eeadaf3a8f%3Ad3c439b9-0267-4e99-8dc3-36f6f0f4d997:ordinal:1", "nodeId": "node:provider:opencode:native-item:prt_1b037f0b5001cDDpsbnPr8Q4Ol", "role": "assistant", "text": "Dragging an item from Active into Pinned should feel like moving it between two persistent lists, not toggling a flag. Show a clear drop zone at the top of the sidebar with a label and insertion indicator, highlight it as the item enters, and place the item at the drop position rather than appending it blindly. The item should visibly leave Active only after a successful drop, with a smooth transition; if the user drops outside a valid zone or cancels, animate it back. Pinned items should support reordering within their section the same way, and dragging a pinned item back into Active should unpin it and insert it at the drop point, preserving order.\n\nBehind the scenes, persist both section membership and order, and keep the two sections internally consistent so a pin doesn't duplicate an item or leave a ghost behind. Handle edge cases explicitly: empty Pinned should show a short hint (\"Drag items here to pin\"), long lists need auto-scroll near the edges, and drag should start only after a small threshold so clicks and context menus still work. Provide a keyboard and menu equivalent (\"Pin\"/\"Unpin\") since drag alone excludes some users, and make sure the same action is available from the item's overflow menu. Keep feedback immediate and reversible\u2014optimistic updates with rollback on failure are better than a silent delay.", "attachments": [], "streaming": false, "createdAt": "2026-11-06T09:36:58.549Z", "updatedAt": "2026-11-06T09:37:18.470Z"}], "plans": [], "turnItems": [{"id": "turn-item:message:message%3Athread%3Athread%253Aproject%253A7b60eb1e-933f-470d-b2e1-b9eeadaf3